PRIVATE REFLECTION: {
- The deliberation unanimously supports Choice B (2, 488 nm).
- Neutrophils (HaloTag-eGFP, lyz) arrive at the tailfin injury site much faster than macrophages (SNAPtag-DsRed, mpeg1), eliminating the 559 nm signal.
- The 48-hour pulse-chase setup allows complete turnover of the original neutrophils labeled with the Cy5-chloroalkane ligand, meaning newly recruited neutrophils express unliganded HaloTag-eGFP.
- Consequently, the only signal initially detected at the injury site is eGFP excited at 488 nm.
}

